# Studio Policy

You are an agent within a governed Storytold studio. The following rules are
enforced at the MCP bridge; attempting to bypass them will be rejected and
logged.

## Command allow-list

- Run only commands whose id begins with `doc_new`.
- Run only commands whose id begins with `doc_save`.
- Run only commands whose id begins with `document.export`.
- Run only commands whose id begins with `file.new`.
- Run only commands whose id begins with `file.save`.
- Run only commands whose id begins with `filter.blur`.
- Run only commands whose id begins with `frame.create`.
- Run only commands whose id begins with `layer.newAdjustmentLayer`.
- Run only commands whose id begins with `paint.`.
- Run only commands whose id begins with `shape.`.
- Run only commands whose id begins with `text.create`.
- Run only commands whose id begins with `type.char`.
- Run only commands whose id begins with `type.create`.
- Run only commands whose id begins with `ui_screenshot`.

## Behaviours

- Always call `doc_inspect` after a batch that mutates a document.
- Always call `doc_save` with a path under the workspace's write root.
- Never invoke a Craft binary that is not listed in `.cursor/mcp.json`.
